WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.980
Good morning Hank, it's Tuesday.

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.740
Specifically it is the 323rd consecutive Tuesday I have made a vlogbrothers video

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:10.500
except for one Tuesday when I had meningitis and another Tuesday when I had a Labyrinthitis

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:15.260
a disease with a very metaphorically resonant name but an extremely low pleasantness factor

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:20.140
What I'm getting at is that I usually upload these videos on time because I am a punctual person

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:23.820
Like I joined conference calls exactly one minute before the call was supposed to begin

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:28.340
I arrived at the doctor's office exactly 15 minutes early in case there's paperwork to fill out

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:33.380
And I must arrive at the airport at least 90 minutes before my flight is scheduled to depart

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:39.120
and when I say must I mean MUST like if I don't there is a five alarm fire in my brain now

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:43.710
There's this line in the Great Gatsby where Nick says everyone suspects himself of at least one of the cardinal virtues

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:44.940
And this is mine

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:47.700
I am one of the few honest people I have ever known

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:49.559
And that's nice Nick, that's a nice sentiment

00:00:49.559 --> 00:00:56.849
but do you show up at Gatsby's house at the exact moment the invitation indicated the party would begin because I would punctuality is the

00:00:57.039 --> 00:01:02.549
Cardinal virtue I suspect myself of I might not be calm I might not be pleasant I might not be good

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:04.170
But I will be on time

00:01:04.170 --> 00:01:11.610
I also really like it when other people value punctuality like rosianna once called punctuality the most important commandment on the tablets

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:13.140
And I'm not sure she was kidding

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:19.830
She's always two minutes early two conference calls to me being punctual is a way of saying to other people I value your time enough

00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:23.429
To show up when we agreed to show up or even slightly earlier

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:27.089
And I think that's important because ultimately time is all we have it is

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:34.349
overwhelmingly the most important human resource you know sometimes you identify so closely with an ideal that it becomes part of how you

00:01:34.630 --> 00:01:38.490
Understand yourself like when I think about Who I am I think I'm a husband

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:44.250
I'm a father and I am a punctual person and once you get to that point like I don't just believe punctuality is

00:01:44.590 --> 00:01:48.329
Unambiguously good. I believe it is inseparable from what constitutes good

00:01:48.430 --> 00:01:52.949
It's difficult to listen to voices that disagree with you let alone take them

00:01:53.110 --> 00:01:53.610
seriously

00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:56.040
Right I mean who could be opposed to punctuality

00:01:56.140 --> 00:02:00.119
E.B White as it turns out who is best known today as the author of Charlotte's Web

00:02:00.119 --> 00:02:02.159
But also was a brilliant magazine writer

00:02:02.159 --> 00:02:06.089
And I was recently reading a collection of his in which he wrote we teach our child many things

00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:09.869
I don't believe in and almost nothing I do believe in we teach punctuality

00:02:10.479 --> 00:02:12.898
particularly if the enforcement of it disturbs the peace

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:19.230
My father taught me by example that the greatest defeat in life was to miss a train only after many years

00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:22.379
Did I learn that an escaping train carries away with it?

00:02:22.379 --> 00:02:29.219
Nothing vital to my health railroad trains are such magnificent objects. We commonly mistake them for destiny

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:34.499
I've always defended my punctuality absolutism by saying it's about respecting other people and their time

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:36.959
But if I'm yelling at my family to get in the car

00:02:36.959 --> 00:02:42.179
So we're not 86 minutes early for a flight am I really respecting people and their time or am

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:44.010
I just disturbing the peace now

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:46.289
I've never missed a train or for that matter of flight

00:02:46.290 --> 00:02:53.340
But until I read those lines it had literally never occurred to me that an escaping train carries with it nothing vital to my health

00:02:53.380 --> 00:02:58.769
But it doesn't of course. I still value punctuality, but lately I've been thinking that as with so many things

00:02:59.380 --> 00:03:04.499
Extreme punctuality can become a vice even when what you worship is good and Noble

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:09.809
It doesn't always make you better or nobler all right. I have to go pack for our Spring Break vacation

00:03:09.810 --> 00:03:15.329
We fly out in the morning. I'm not gonna miss the flight or anything, but I am gonna try to be less early Hank

00:03:15.370 --> 00:03:17.370
I'll see you on Friday

